715
00:48:41,711 --> 00:48:43,336
(SCHOOL BELL RlNGlNG)

716
00:48:48,342 --> 00:48:51,469
-You got a second?
-What, did l do something wrong?

717
00:48:51,554 --> 00:48:54,556
No. You did a great job on your book report.

718
00:48:56,309 --> 00:48:59,436
You really seemed to like the book,
The Count of Monte Cristo.

719
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:03,273
lt's my favorite.
l liked it more since l've been in here.

720
00:49:03,357 --> 00:49:04,858
Why is that?

721
00:49:05,818 --> 00:49:09,404
lt's like, he wouldn't let anyone beat him,
the Count.

722
00:49:10,239 --> 00:49:14,075
Took what he had to take,
beatings, insults, and whatever.

723
00:49:15,077 --> 00:49:16,911
And he learned from it.

724
00:49:16,996 --> 00:49:21,291
Then when the time came for him
to do something, he made his move.

725
00:49:22,001 --> 00:49:24,878
-You admire that?
-No, l respect that.

726
00:49:27,048 --> 00:49:29,382
You got a copy of the book at home?

727
00:49:29,467 --> 00:49:32,260
l got the Classics lllustrated Comic.

728
00:49:32,345 --> 00:49:33,970
lt's not the same thing.

729
00:49:34,055 --> 00:49:36,598
Listen, l gotta go.
l'm gonna miss morning roll call.

730
00:49:36,682 --> 00:49:39,768
Wait one minute. l've got something for you.

731
00:49:41,395 --> 00:49:44,731
-l thought you might like to have it.
-SHAKES: Are you serious?

732
00:49:44,815 --> 00:49:48,318
You love the book that much.
You should have a copy of your own.

733
00:49:48,402 --> 00:49:50,820
-l can't pay you.
-lt's a gift.

734
00:49:51,656 --> 00:49:55,325
-You've gotten gifts before, haven't you?
-lt's been a while.

735
00:49:55,409 --> 00:49:58,662
-lt's my way of saying thanks.
-For what?

736
00:50:00,039 --> 00:50:03,375
That somebody listens,
even if it's just one student.

737
00:50:03,459 --> 00:50:05,168
You're a good teacher, Mr. Carlson.

738
00:50:05,252 --> 00:50:07,337
We can discuss the book on Friday in class

739
00:50:07,421 --> 00:50:09,673
if you think the Count
can hold their attention.

740
00:50:09,757 --> 00:50:11,174
He's got a shot.

741
00:50:11,258 --> 00:50:13,468
Any particular section l should read from?

742
00:50:13,552 --> 00:50:16,971
That's easy.
The part where he escapes from prison.

743
00:50:29,735 --> 00:50:32,696
There you go, star. Here's your locker room.

744
00:50:40,121 --> 00:50:44,749
SHAKES: It was only a game,
just a touch football game, nothing more.

745
00:50:45,584 --> 00:50:48,002
But a game I wish we had never played.

746
00:50:48,087 --> 00:50:52,048
Guards against inmates.
The guards practiced four times a week.

747
00:50:52,925 --> 00:50:55,802
Our team was picked
the Monday before the game.

748
00:50:55,886 --> 00:50:59,472
We had a two-hour practice.
It didn't matter much.

749
00:50:59,557 --> 00:51:03,518
We weren't supposed to win.
We were just supposed to show up.

750
00:51:03,602 --> 00:51:07,397
-Who's the toughest guy out here?
-How do you mean, tough?

751
00:51:07,648 --> 00:51:12,068
-Who can talk and have everyone listen?
-Rizzo. Black kid over there.

752
00:51:13,529 --> 00:51:17,115
SHAKES: Michael saw an opening,
a chance to bring the game to our level,

753
00:51:17,199 --> 00:51:21,327
even out the field.
But he needed help. He needed Rizzo.

754
00:51:21,954 --> 00:51:26,207
Black kid with an Italian name.
With Rizzo on our side, we had a chance.

755
00:51:27,084 --> 00:51:29,961
Look, white boy,
l don't know what you play in the streets.

756
00:51:30,045 --> 00:51:32,630
l don't care.
But in here, the guards call the play

757
00:51:32,715 --> 00:51:35,717
-and the play calls for them to win the game.
-Why?

758
00:51:36,635 --> 00:51:40,221
Guards steer clear of me, all right?
They stay back and let me do my time.

759
00:51:40,306 --> 00:51:44,058
lf l play that game and hurt one of them,
they just might change my cushion.

760
00:51:44,143 --> 00:51:47,854
MlCHAEL: I'm not saying we gotta win.
I just don't want to take a beating.

761
00:51:47,938 --> 00:51:49,481
RlZZO: You do, every day.

762
00:51:49,565 --> 00:51:53,485
-Why is Saturday special?
-'Cause on Saturday, we can hit back.

763
00:51:55,529 --> 00:51:59,532
They don't fuck with you like they do us,
but they fuck with you in another way.

764
00:51:59,617 --> 00:52:01,534
You're just an animal to them.

765
00:52:01,619 --> 00:52:04,204
-l don't give a fuck.
-Yeah, you do.

766
00:52:04,455 --> 00:52:07,916
And beating them on Saturday
is not gonna change a thing.

767
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,417
Then why, white boy?

768
00:52:09,502 --> 00:52:13,922
To make them feel what we feel.
Just for a couple of hours.

769
00:52:15,966 --> 00:52:17,926
Now, don't try anything funny, Sambo.

770
00:52:18,010 --> 00:52:20,470
Nobody will get hurt.
You know what l'm saying?

771
00:52:20,554 --> 00:52:22,931
-l call heads.
-REFEREE: He calls heads.

772
00:52:24,558 --> 00:52:26,893
REFEREE: He called heads. lt is a head.

773
00:52:28,729 --> 00:52:30,063
Let's go.

774
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:33,650
(PLAYERS GRUNTlNG)

775
00:52:35,986 --> 00:52:37,403
(NOKES GRUNTlNG lN PAlN)

776
00:52:39,782 --> 00:52:43,576
You're gonna die, motherfucker.
You're gonna fucking die.

777
00:52:43,661 --> 00:52:45,620
(PLAYERS GRUNTlNG)

778
00:52:53,754 --> 00:52:55,755
None of you motherfuckers can cover me!

779
00:52:55,840 --> 00:52:59,342
We got ourselves a game!
l'm feeling good today.

780
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:01,636
This shit feels good.

781
00:53:14,191 --> 00:53:15,233
GUARD 1: Fuck!

782
00:53:15,317 --> 00:53:16,860
GUARD 2: Get the fuck off of me!

783
00:53:29,373 --> 00:53:31,875
Yeah, keep smiling, you little pissant.

784
00:53:34,670 --> 00:53:37,755
SHAKES: For 90 minutes,
we took the game out of the prison,

785
00:53:37,840 --> 00:53:39,757
moved it miles beyond the locked gates

786
00:53:39,842 --> 00:53:42,677
and the sloping hills
of the surrounding countryside,

787
00:53:42,761 --> 00:53:46,681
and brought it back down to the streets
of the neighborhoods we'd come from.

788
00:53:46,765 --> 00:53:49,893
For those 90 minutes,
we were once again free.

789
00:53:49,977 --> 00:53:52,353
(PLAYERS YELLlNG)

790
00:53:55,774 --> 00:53:58,484
(lNMATES CHEERlNG)

791
00:54:00,946 --> 00:54:02,363
(WHOOPlNG)

792
00:54:06,076 --> 00:54:09,245
lNMATES: (CHANTlNG) Rizzo! Rizzo!

793
00:54:13,542 --> 00:54:15,168
(CHANTlNG CONTlNUES)

794
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:23,092
(SOFTLY) Rizzo.

795
00:54:27,598 --> 00:54:30,767
Nokes, good game.

796
00:54:33,604 --> 00:54:36,940
SHAKES: For once, we had a victory.
But it didn't last.

797
00:54:37,524 --> 00:54:39,233
It couldn't last.

798
00:54:39,860 --> 00:54:42,320
And all I wanted to do was die.

799
00:54:42,988 --> 00:54:44,781
I was not alone in the hole.

800
00:54:44,865 --> 00:54:47,533
I knew my friends
were down in the depths with me.

801
00:54:47,618 --> 00:54:52,080
Each in his own cell, each in his own pain,
suffering his own demons.

802
00:54:52,289 --> 00:54:54,207
Rizzo was there, too.

803
00:54:56,627 --> 00:54:58,920
I had lost any sense of time.

804
00:55:17,815 --> 00:55:19,190
(LAUGHlNG)

805
00:55:38,919 --> 00:55:41,295
l thought you'd never wake up.

806
00:55:41,380 --> 00:55:43,256
SHAKES: l thought l'd never want to.

807
00:55:43,340 --> 00:55:46,551
John and Tommy,
they're on the other side there.

808
00:55:47,970 --> 00:55:49,470
How are they?

809
00:55:50,973 --> 00:55:52,473
They're alive.

810
00:55:53,434 --> 00:55:54,851
Who isn't?

811
00:55:56,478 --> 00:55:57,770
Rizzo.

812
00:56:00,149 --> 00:56:01,858
They killed him?

813
00:56:03,235 --> 00:56:07,655
They took turns beating him
until there was nothing of that kid to beat.

814
00:56:12,202 --> 00:56:14,495
SHAKES: Rizzo was dead because of us.

815
00:56:14,705 --> 00:56:17,290
We made him think
that going up against the guards

816
00:56:17,374 --> 00:56:20,543
in a meaningless football game
had some value,

817
00:56:20,627 --> 00:56:23,337
that it would give us a reason to go on.

818
00:56:23,422 --> 00:56:25,506
Once again, we were wrong.

819
00:56:28,510 --> 00:56:30,178
TOMMY: Did they give you a release date yet?

820
00:56:30,262 --> 00:56:31,929
SHAKES: Nokes had a letter from the warden.

821
00:56:32,014 --> 00:56:34,724
Waved it in front of me, then tore it up.

822
00:56:35,184 --> 00:56:37,018
MlCHAEL: When do you figure?

823
00:56:37,144 --> 00:56:40,897
l don't know. End of spring,
early summer, or something.

824
00:56:41,106 --> 00:56:43,566
l wish we were coming with you.

825
00:56:43,650 --> 00:56:47,195
lt would've been nice
for all of us to walk out together.

826
00:56:47,279 --> 00:56:51,783
No use thinking about that.
We're gonna do a full year, not an hour less.

827
00:56:52,826 --> 00:56:56,370
When l get out, l could get Father Bobby
to make a couple of phone calls.

828
00:56:56,455 --> 00:56:57,663
Shave a month or two off.

829
00:56:57,748 --> 00:57:01,042
-There's nothing to talk about.
-There's a lot to talk about.

830
00:57:01,126 --> 00:57:04,545
Maybe if people knew what was going on
in here, they'd make a move.

831
00:57:04,630 --> 00:57:06,964
l don't want anybody to know.

832
00:57:07,049 --> 00:57:10,718
Not Father Bobby, King Benny, Fat Mancho,

833
00:57:10,803 --> 00:57:13,096
not my mother. Nobody.

834
00:57:14,765 --> 00:57:16,099
TOMMY: Yeah, l don't, either.

835
00:57:16,183 --> 00:57:19,352
l mean, l wouldn't know
what to say to anyone who did know.

836
00:57:19,436 --> 00:57:22,855
MlCHAEL: l can't think of anybody
who needs to hear about it.

837
00:57:23,190 --> 00:57:26,734
Either they won't believe it,
or they won't give a shit.

838
00:57:26,819 --> 00:57:30,446
Yeah, l don't even think we should
talk about it once it's over.

839
00:57:31,323 --> 00:57:35,868
We got no choice but to live with it.
And talking makes living it harder.

840
00:57:36,703 --> 00:57:39,539
So we might as well not even talk about it.

841
00:57:39,623 --> 00:57:41,749
The truth stays with us.

842
00:57:44,545 --> 00:57:47,380
l want to be able to sleep one night

843
00:57:47,881 --> 00:57:52,385
and not have to worry who's coming
in my room, what's gonna happen to me.

844
00:57:55,055 --> 00:57:59,100
lf l can get that, then l'll be happy.

845
00:58:01,895 --> 00:58:04,438
Someday, John. l promise.

846
00:58:21,415 --> 00:58:25,126
SHAKES: I was in my last hours as an inmate
at the Wilkinson Home for Boys.

847
00:58:25,419 --> 00:58:30,256
I was given four copies of my release form.
The final reminder of my time at Wilkinson.

848
00:58:32,176 --> 00:58:34,719
I never heard the key turn in the lock

849
00:58:34,803 --> 00:58:37,763
and I never heard the snap of the bolt.

850
00:58:38,599 --> 00:58:40,516
NOKES: You should be asleep.

851
00:58:40,976 --> 00:58:44,937
l just wanted to say good-bye. We all do.

852
00:58:47,983 --> 00:58:49,609
NOKES: l told him right to his face.

853
00:58:49,693 --> 00:58:52,111
l said, "l don't care
if you're paying me overtime.

854
00:58:52,196 --> 00:58:53,863
"l'm not working those kind of hours."

855
00:58:53,947 --> 00:58:56,449
FERGUSON: Yeah, but you put in for it?
NOKES: Yeah, l did.

856
00:58:56,533 --> 00:58:59,076
FERGUSON: 'Cause l put in for it,
and they don't give it.

857
00:58:59,161 --> 00:59:02,705
l come in early for three days,
do they give me overtime? No.

858
00:59:03,290 --> 00:59:06,209
SHAKES: A part of all of us
was left there that night.

859
00:59:06,293 --> 00:59:09,253
A night that will
never be removed from my mind.

860
00:59:09,338 --> 00:59:14,008
That night of June 1, 1968,
the summer of love.

861
00:59:15,302 --> 00:59:18,387
My last night
at the Wilkinson Home for Boys.

862
00:59:37,658 --> 00:59:40,117
(CARS HONKlNG)

863
01:00:04,101 --> 01:00:07,270
SHAKES: At 8:25 p.m.,
two men walked through the doors.

864
01:00:07,354 --> 01:00:11,148
The bartender knew their faces as most
of the neighborhood knew their names.

865
01:00:11,233 --> 01:00:14,193
They were two of the founding members
of the West Side Boys.

866
01:00:14,278 --> 01:00:16,570
They were also its deadliest.

867
01:00:17,364 --> 01:00:21,075
The blond-haired man had been
in and out of jail since he was a teenager.

868
01:00:21,201 --> 01:00:23,953
He robbed and killed at will, or on command.

869
01:00:24,037 --> 01:00:27,164
He's presently a suspect
in four unsolved homicides.

870
01:00:27,249 --> 01:00:31,335
He was an alcoholic and a cocaine abuser
with a fast temper and a faster trigger.

871
01:00:31,420 --> 01:00:35,881
He once shot a mechanic dead
for moving ahead of him in a movie line.

872
01:00:36,383 --> 01:00:38,467
The dark-haired man was equally deadly,

873
01:00:38,552 --> 01:00:41,595
and had committed his first murder
at the age of 17.

874
01:00:41,722 --> 01:00:43,889
In return, he was paid $50.

875
01:00:44,224 --> 01:00:45,725
He drank and he did drugs

876
01:00:45,809 --> 01:00:49,729
and he had a wife he never saw,
living somewhere in Queens.

877
01:00:55,902 --> 01:00:57,486
(MEN CHATTERlNG)

878
01:00:58,238 --> 01:01:02,325
-lt'll take more than four years to get...
-They'll take it at the mid-term elections.

879
01:01:02,409 --> 01:01:05,202
BUSlNESSMAN 1: He's got the charisma.
He's gonna do it.

880
01:01:05,287 --> 01:01:08,164
BUSlNESSMAN 2: He's our man.
Reagan's the man who's gonna do it.

881
01:01:09,499 --> 01:01:12,293
Hey, Jerry. Who are they talking about?

882
01:01:12,419 --> 01:01:15,087
They're talking about Reagan's speech.

883
01:01:17,299 --> 01:01:20,634
Order those two men some drinks
and put it on my tab.

884
01:01:21,595 --> 01:01:24,764
Tell them that Republicans
are not welcome in Hell's Kitchen,

885
01:01:24,848 --> 01:01:28,851
and either a political conversion
or a change of conversation is in order.

886
01:01:28,935 --> 01:01:30,436
Sure thing.

887
01:01:33,940 --> 01:01:35,983
-Gentlemen.
-Yeah?

888
01:01:36,651 --> 01:01:39,987
The gentlemen there would like to
buy you a drink on one condition.

889
01:01:40,113 --> 01:01:43,783
You know the rules, no religion, no politics.

890
01:01:44,451 --> 01:01:46,285
You get my meaning?

891
01:01:54,252 --> 01:01:56,295
(MAN CHATTERlNG ON TV)

892
01:02:03,136 --> 01:02:06,514
Order something for me.
l gotta go to the bathroom.

893
01:02:27,661 --> 01:02:29,703
(METALLlC CLANKlNG)

894
01:02:36,503 --> 01:02:39,171
Can l help you with something, chief?

895
01:02:39,506 --> 01:02:41,090
Not right now.

896
01:02:42,551 --> 01:02:44,844
Enjoy the rest of your meal.

897
01:03:30,932 --> 01:03:34,935
l ordered brisket on a roll with fries

898
01:03:35,562 --> 01:03:39,315
and two baskets of soda bread.
l know how you like that shit.

899
01:03:39,399 --> 01:03:41,275
ls that okay by you?

900
01:03:42,652 --> 01:03:46,322
Take a look at the guy at the table.
Take a good look.

901
01:03:57,584 --> 01:03:59,126
Motherfucker.

902
01:04:25,320 --> 01:04:26,779
That's him.

903
01:04:27,239 --> 01:04:29,490
Are you fucking kidding me?

904
01:04:32,285 --> 01:04:33,494
Bingo.

905
01:04:58,478 --> 01:05:00,145
This is amazing.

906
01:05:00,480 --> 01:05:02,815
Hello. lt's been a long time.

907
01:05:04,276 --> 01:05:06,360
Who the fuck are you guys?

908
01:05:09,823 --> 01:05:11,740
Who the fuck asked you to sit down?

909
01:05:11,825 --> 01:05:15,619
l thought you'd be happy to see us.
l guess l was wrong.

910
01:05:16,830 --> 01:05:19,290
JOHN: l thought you'd do a lot better.

911
01:05:19,791 --> 01:05:22,751
With all that training,
all that time you put in,

912
01:05:22,836 --> 01:05:25,045
just to end up watching
someone else's money.

913
01:05:25,171 --> 01:05:26,338
That seems like a waste.

914
01:05:26,464 --> 01:05:28,549
For the last time,
what the fuck do you want?

915
01:05:28,675 --> 01:05:31,885
Why don't you take your time?
lt'll come to you.

916
01:05:36,182 --> 01:05:38,559
l can see how he might forget us.

917
01:05:38,685 --> 01:05:41,645
We were just something
for you and your friends to play with.

918
01:05:41,730 --> 01:05:46,525
lt's a little harder for us to forget.
You gave us so much more to remember.

919
01:05:49,821 --> 01:05:53,782
You can't quite place us, can you, chief?
Let me help you out.

920
01:05:53,867 --> 01:05:57,244
You're looking at John Reilly
and Tommy Marcano.

921
01:06:03,168 --> 01:06:04,376
Yeah.

922
01:06:07,380 --> 01:06:08,922
That's right.

923
01:06:15,388 --> 01:06:17,514
That was a long time ago.

924
01:06:19,893 --> 01:06:21,727
So, how you been?

925
01:06:21,895 --> 01:06:23,896
Yeah, we ain't kids now.

926
01:06:24,022 --> 01:06:26,065
So what do you want?

927
01:06:27,025 --> 01:06:30,069
What l've always wanted is to watch you die.

928
01:06:36,076 --> 01:06:38,118
TOMMY: You ordered the meatloaf.

929
01:06:38,912 --> 01:06:42,748
The brisket's really good here,
only you'll never know it.

930
01:06:43,041 --> 01:06:44,583
You fucked up.

931
01:06:57,764 --> 01:07:02,101
You were scared little pricks, both of you.

932
01:07:03,603 --> 01:07:07,815
All of you, scared shitless.

933
01:07:10,151 --> 01:07:13,737
l tried to make you tough.
l tried to make you hard.

934
01:07:13,822 --> 01:07:15,489
TOMMY: l had you all wrong then, Nokes.

935
01:07:15,615 --> 01:07:19,201
All this time l thought you just liked
fucking and beating up little boys.

936
01:07:19,285 --> 01:07:22,079
You two motherfuckers
are gonna burn in hell.

937
01:07:22,163 --> 01:07:25,290
-You're gonna burn in hell.
-Yeah, after you.

938
01:07:26,876 --> 01:07:28,210
(GASPlNG)

939
01:07:28,294 --> 01:07:30,254
(GROANlNG)

940
01:07:30,338 --> 01:07:32,297
Did that hurt, Nokes?

941
01:07:57,657 --> 01:07:59,324
(CRYlNG)

942
01:08:08,835 --> 01:08:10,169
Jerry.

943
01:08:10,837 --> 01:08:14,381
Sorry, should've made
those brisket sandwiches to go.

944
01:08:19,179 --> 01:08:21,054
(PATRONS SCREAMlNG)

945
01:08:25,810 --> 01:08:29,438
JUDGE: John Reilly, how do you plead?
JOHN: Not guilty, Your Honor.

946
01:08:29,522 --> 01:08:31,190
JUDGE: Thomas Marcano?

947
01:08:31,900 --> 01:08:33,609
TOMMY: Not guilty, Your Honor.

948
01:08:33,693 --> 01:08:37,863
JUDGE: John Reilly and Thomas Marcano,
you are hereby held without bail.

949
01:08:38,406 --> 01:08:42,242
SHAKES: In all the years since Wilkinson's,
we had never once spoken to each other

950
01:08:42,368 --> 01:08:43,994
about what had happened there.

951
01:08:44,078 --> 01:08:47,831
We remained caring friends,
but the relationship had been altered.

952
01:08:48,833 --> 01:08:53,212
We drifted together, always wondering
if that moment would arrive

953
01:08:53,421 --> 01:08:56,381
that would force us to deal with the past.

954
01:09:08,895 --> 01:09:12,272
One down, Shakes.

955
01:09:14,192 --> 01:09:15,526
One what?

956
01:09:17,111 --> 01:09:20,447
One Sean Nokes.

957
01:09:21,533 --> 01:09:22,658
Nokes?

958
01:09:30,792 --> 01:09:32,334
SHAKES: At the time of Nokes' shooting,

959
01:09:32,418 --> 01:09:35,796
Michael was working
as an Assistant New York District Attorney.

960
01:09:35,922 --> 01:09:40,926
I got a call that he wanted to meet me
on 45th Street in Queens, then he hung up.

961
01:09:44,931 --> 01:09:46,682
-MlCHAEL: So what did they say?
-What?

962
01:09:46,766 --> 01:09:50,477
-John and Tommy, what'd they say?
-lt's a little cloak and dagger, isn't it?

963
01:09:50,603 --> 01:09:53,397
Come on. Nokes. Did they talk about him?

964
01:09:54,482 --> 01:09:57,776
-John did.
-Yeah? What did he say?

965
01:09:58,611 --> 01:10:01,154
He said, "One down, Shakes."

966
01:10:04,617 --> 01:10:06,827
l hear they hired Danny Snyder
as the lawyer.

967
01:10:06,953 --> 01:10:09,913
lt's temporary. King Benny's gonna move in
one of his lawyers.

968
01:10:09,998 --> 01:10:14,126
-Don't let him do that. Snyder's perfect.
-Perfect? The guy's a fall-down drunk.

969
01:10:14,252 --> 01:10:16,628
-He's perfect.
-Perfect for what?

970
01:10:20,466 --> 01:10:22,634
Are you covering this story
for your newspaper?

971
01:10:22,719 --> 01:10:23,886
-Me?
-Yeah.

972
01:10:23,970 --> 01:10:27,556
l'm a timetable clerk, Mikey.
Ask me what movie's playing at what time.

973
01:10:27,640 --> 01:10:29,975
l'm lucky they let me in the building.

974
01:10:33,813 --> 01:10:35,480
Get some coffee?

975
01:10:35,607 --> 01:10:37,316
Let's take a walk.

976
01:10:47,619 --> 01:10:50,662
l'm gonna prosecute John and Tommy
in an open court.

977
01:10:51,080 --> 01:10:54,416
-What are you, fucking nuts?
-Just hear me out.

978
01:10:54,500 --> 01:10:57,419
Stay home tomorrow.
Call in sick and save your life, Counsel.

979
01:10:57,503 --> 01:10:59,922
l'm not taking this case to win.

980
01:11:00,757 --> 01:11:03,008
l'm taking this case to lose.

981
01:11:03,468 --> 01:11:05,344
What does that mean?

982
01:11:07,013 --> 01:11:09,181
lt means it's payback time.

983
01:11:09,515 --> 01:11:13,936
Look, John and Tommy started this.
lt's begun.

984
01:11:14,771 --> 01:11:18,357
lt's messy, it's not how l had it planned,
but here it is.

985
01:11:19,984 --> 01:11:24,154
-And you and l, we can finish it.
-Finish what, Mikey?

986
01:11:26,950 --> 01:11:29,952
You read The Count of Monte Cristo lately?

987
01:11:30,203 --> 01:11:32,621
l don't know, 10 years ago.

988
01:11:33,790 --> 01:11:37,000
You see, l read a little bit of it every night.

989
01:11:37,210 --> 01:11:41,463
l read words like "revenge."
"Sweet, lasting revenge."

990
01:11:43,549 --> 01:11:47,636
Payback time. lt's our time.

991
01:11:49,138 --> 01:11:50,889
What are you saying?

992
01:11:51,391 --> 01:11:54,810
l'm saying it's time for all of us
to get a taste.

993
01:11:55,728 --> 01:11:58,855
l'm saying it's time to put an end to this.

994
01:12:00,233 --> 01:12:01,733
Let's walk.

995
01:12:04,904 --> 01:12:06,154
So l asked for the case.

996
01:12:06,239 --> 01:12:09,157
Told them l was from the same
neighborhood as the accused,

997
01:12:09,242 --> 01:12:10,909
knew the mentality of the area.

998
01:12:10,994 --> 01:12:12,411
They bought it.

999
01:12:12,537 --> 01:12:14,913
And the connection between
John, Tommy, and Nokes?

1000
01:12:14,998 --> 01:12:18,917
What connection? All juvenile records
are destroyed after seven years.

1001
01:12:19,043 --> 01:12:21,336
We were never at Wilkinson's.

1002
01:12:24,090 --> 01:12:27,592
l gotta go after the guards.
l gotta get Wilkinson's.

1003
01:12:28,094 --> 01:12:29,678
Bring it all down.

1004
01:12:29,762 --> 01:12:33,098
MlCHAEL: Adam Styler, plainclothes cop.
Works narcotics in Queens.

1005
01:12:33,182 --> 01:12:36,935
Known to shake down dealers for dope
and cash. He's got a cocaine problem.

1006
01:12:37,020 --> 01:12:38,687
Other personal information there.

1007
01:12:38,771 --> 01:12:42,607
Henry Addison. Now works for the mayor,
if you can fucking believe that.

1008
01:12:42,692 --> 01:12:44,776
He's a Community Outreach Director
in Brooklyn.

1009
01:12:44,902 --> 01:12:48,864
His sexual habits haven't changed.
He still likes sex with young boys.

1010
01:12:48,948 --> 01:12:52,284
Ralph Ferguson. Works in a social service
agency in Long lsland.

1011
01:12:52,410 --> 01:12:54,202
How long you been working on this?

1012
01:12:54,287 --> 01:12:56,121
He's recently divorced, got one child,

1013
01:12:56,247 --> 01:12:58,540
and on weekends,
teaches Catholic Sunday school.

1014
01:12:58,624 --> 01:13:02,544
-He seems clean then, right?
-That's exactly why l want the piece of shit.

1015
01:13:02,628 --> 01:13:05,213
The plan is to call Ferguson
in as a character witness.

1016
01:13:05,298 --> 01:13:08,050
Get him talking about his best friend,
Sean Nokes.

1017
01:13:08,134 --> 01:13:12,471
Once l got him on the stand,
l'm gonna open the door to Wilkinson's.

1018
01:13:12,555 --> 01:13:16,767
Mike, are you sure you want to go this way?

1019
01:13:20,480 --> 01:13:23,273
l mean, we buried this a long time ago.

1020
01:13:24,942 --> 01:13:27,652
Do you still sleep with the light on?

1021
01:13:32,116 --> 01:13:35,327
John and Tommy, do you want them
to know anything about this?

1022
01:13:35,453 --> 01:13:38,830
No, it'll play better in court
if they don't know.

1023
01:13:49,926 --> 01:13:53,929
SHAKES: The "not guilty" verdict had to be
a verdict that no one would dare question.

1024
01:13:54,013 --> 01:13:57,682
Danny Snyder was to remain
as Tommy and John's attorney.

1025
01:13:58,017 --> 01:14:00,352
Michael's plan relied heavily
on Hell's Kitchen

1026
01:14:00,436 --> 01:14:02,437
to deliver information and keep quiet.

1027
01:14:02,522 --> 01:14:05,273
Both were skills
the neighborhood had in abundance.

1028
01:14:05,358 --> 01:14:07,776
We'd set up a simple method
of communication.

1029
01:14:07,860 --> 01:14:10,445
If Michael was sending,
messages were left at work

1030
01:14:10,530 --> 01:14:13,115
for me to call
my non-existent girlfriend, Gloria.

1031
01:14:13,199 --> 01:14:16,618
If I needed to get word to Michael,
someone from the neighborhood

1032
01:14:16,702 --> 01:14:19,287
would pick up an early edition
of The New York Times,

1033
01:14:19,372 --> 01:14:22,791
write "Edmund" in the upper
right hand corner of the Metro section,

1034
01:14:22,875 --> 01:14:25,210
and drop it in front of Michael's apartment.

1035
01:14:29,215 --> 01:14:30,465
For this plan to succeed

1036
01:14:30,550 --> 01:14:33,718
we needed total secrecy
of the only people we completely trusted.

1037
01:14:33,845 --> 01:14:35,887
The plan depended on keeping Michael alive,

1038
01:14:35,972 --> 01:14:38,974
which meant word had to get
to John and Tommy's killing crew

1039
01:14:39,058 --> 01:14:40,392
that he's not an open target.

1040
01:14:40,518 --> 01:14:43,728
After this night,
Michael would not be available to any of us.

1041
01:14:43,855 --> 01:14:46,815
The only time we would see him
would be in court.

1042
01:14:46,899 --> 01:14:48,817
-That's it?
-Not quite.

1043
01:14:48,901 --> 01:14:52,070
Four witnesses saw the shooting
and are willing to testify.

1044
01:14:52,155 --> 01:14:53,655
We gotta get that number down.

1045
01:14:53,739 --> 01:14:56,324
-l'll talk to King Benny.
-Good.

1046
01:14:57,034 --> 01:15:00,745
l can handle two,
but you gotta get us one for our side.

1047
01:15:01,038 --> 01:15:03,248
-One of what?
-One witness.

1048
01:15:03,749 --> 01:15:07,586
A witness who'll put John and Tommy
somewhere else on the night of the murder.

1049
01:15:07,670 --> 01:15:09,838
A witness they can't touch.

1050
01:15:10,590 --> 01:15:14,259
-Don't they have a name for that?
-A judge would call it perjury.

1051
01:15:14,343 --> 01:15:15,760
(LAUGHS)

1052
01:15:15,845 --> 01:15:18,597
-And what are we calling it?
-A favor.

1053
01:15:22,185 --> 01:15:23,435
Get up.

1054
01:15:26,606 --> 01:15:28,398
-Tony?
-Yeah, King?

1055
01:15:28,524 --> 01:15:32,611
-Bring Danny Snyder to see me.
-Who, Danny Snyder the lawyer?

1056
01:15:32,695 --> 01:15:35,363
-You know more than one Danny Snyder?
-No, King.

1057
01:15:35,448 --> 01:15:37,616
Bring me the one you know.

1058
01:15:56,052 --> 01:16:00,639
l can't do this now, you gotta know that.
lt's been a long time for me.

1059
01:16:02,725 --> 01:16:06,311
You need somebody younger.
Somebody like l used to be.

1060
01:16:06,437 --> 01:16:08,313
KlNG BENNY: Younger is not better.

1061
01:16:08,397 --> 01:16:11,983
Doesn't have experience, doesn't
know its way around a courthouse.

1062
01:16:12,068 --> 01:16:14,444
l'm lucky l can find the courthouse.

1063
01:16:15,655 --> 01:16:19,407
l had only four cases last year.
You know how many l won?

1064
01:16:20,159 --> 01:16:22,827
None. That's how many.

1065
01:16:24,330 --> 01:16:29,000
ln two of them,
l think the jury blamed me personally.

1066
01:16:29,418 --> 01:16:31,503
They must've been innocent.

1067
01:16:32,088 --> 01:16:34,965
lt's tough to get innocent men off a rap.

1068
01:16:35,341 --> 01:16:37,968
l wasn't even planning on
going to court with this one.

1069
01:16:38,052 --> 01:16:40,845
l was just gonna plea it down
best l could, and walk away.

1070
01:16:40,930 --> 01:16:44,099
l wasn't planning on taking this to trial, sir.

1071
01:16:44,183 --> 01:16:46,434
Your plans have been changed.

1072
01:16:46,519 --> 01:16:50,647
l am afraid that l'll make a mistake
and say the wrong thing,

1073
01:16:52,733 --> 01:16:56,111
make a wrong turn somewhere.
You don't want to take that risk.

1074
01:16:56,195 --> 01:16:58,613
-Life is risk.
-l'm sorry?

1075
01:16:59,115 --> 01:17:01,825
-Life is risk.
-Life is a risk?

1076
01:17:06,622 --> 01:17:08,915
l haven't been in here before.

1077
01:17:10,167 --> 01:17:12,669
-What do you need me to do?
-Listen.

1078
01:17:12,753 --> 01:17:16,298
You're gonna be given the answers
and the questions.

1079
01:17:17,300 --> 01:17:20,760
All you have to do is read.
You can read, can't you?

1080
01:17:22,013 --> 01:17:23,555
ls it in English?

1081
01:17:23,639 --> 01:17:26,433
Just don't drift. Don't drink, and don't lose.

1082
01:17:28,019 --> 01:17:31,771
-What if l do lose?
-Then you go down for the dirt nap.

1083
01:17:32,940 --> 01:17:35,567
Never heard that expression before.

1084
01:17:36,777 --> 01:17:38,278
Dirt nap.

1085
01:17:39,613 --> 01:17:43,908
l'm not really cut out for this anymore.
l mean, a guy gets hit by a bus

1086
01:17:44,744 --> 01:17:47,162
and sues, l like that.

1087
01:17:47,246 --> 01:17:51,458
Some lady slips in a supermarket,
l'm with her.

1088
01:17:51,542 --> 01:17:53,084
The discussion is over.

1089
01:17:53,169 --> 01:17:57,047
l'm an alcoholic.
This is a murder case. This isn't for me.

1090
01:17:57,340 --> 01:17:59,382
-lt was, once.
-Yes, but...

1091
01:17:59,467 --> 01:18:01,801
Before you let the drink lead.

1092
01:18:02,803 --> 01:18:06,473
Be sober by tomorrow.
And don't look so worried, Snyder.

1093
01:18:06,807 --> 01:18:09,934
You've got nothing to lose,
just like the rest of us.

1094
01:18:10,019 --> 01:18:13,480
l don't want to be a burden to you,
but aside...

1095
01:18:14,315 --> 01:18:18,485
Or along with my alcohol problem,
l have a slight drug problem.

1096
01:18:18,569 --> 01:18:21,237
-Nothing big, just...
-Go away.

1097
01:18:32,333 --> 01:18:34,334
SHAKES: Within days
of Michael taking the case,

1098
01:18:34,418 --> 01:18:36,836
the West Side Boys got a visit
from King Benny.

1099
01:18:36,921 --> 01:18:40,632
The King requested that the verbal abuse
directed towards Michael continue.

1100
01:18:40,716 --> 01:18:44,135
Cries of "traitor" and "gutter rat"
were heard up and down the avenue.

1101
01:18:44,220 --> 01:18:46,763
But there was never to be
a death move against him.

1102
01:18:46,847 --> 01:18:49,349
The hit on Michael Sullivan,
if there was to be one,

1103
01:18:49,433 --> 01:18:51,017
could only come from King Benny.

1104
01:18:51,102 --> 01:18:53,561
The underground word,
the only one that mattered,

1105
01:18:53,646 --> 01:18:57,315
had spread through the streets
at the speed of a late-night bullet.

1106
01:19:00,986 --> 01:19:04,072
King Benny's sleepers
were making their play.

1107
01:19:04,156 --> 01:19:08,076
"Sleepers" was a street name for anyone
who spent time in a juvenile facility.

1108
01:19:17,628 --> 01:19:20,880
You gonna pay for that, you little prick?

1109
01:19:20,965 --> 01:19:23,341
SHAKES: Need your help, Fat Man.
Need a big favor.

1110
01:19:23,426 --> 01:19:24,592
See you outside.

1111
01:19:25,344 --> 01:19:28,304
-King Benny been to see you?
-My goodness.

1112
01:19:28,389 --> 01:19:30,682
What a fucking team we put together, huh?

1113
01:19:30,766 --> 01:19:35,019
You have a drunk lawyer on one side,
a kid lawyer on the other.

1114
01:19:35,396 --> 01:19:38,398
Fucking paper boy, making like Dick Tracy.

1115
01:19:38,941 --> 01:19:42,694
There are four sets of eyeballs
that saw the whole thing.

1116
01:19:42,945 --> 01:19:46,197
Meanwhile, the two on trial
kill more people than cancer.

1117
01:19:46,282 --> 01:19:48,658
Fucking General Custer
has a better shot at a walk.

1118
01:19:48,742 --> 01:19:50,785
SHAKES: There's no connection
with the guard and us.

1119
01:19:50,870 --> 01:19:52,704
Cops think it's a drug-related homicide.

1120
01:19:52,788 --> 01:19:54,789
lt's just we need you to pull a few strings.

1121
01:19:54,874 --> 01:19:58,251
lf you get caught on this,
you're looking straight-ass serious.

1122
01:19:58,335 --> 01:20:01,087
l'm talking real jail. The big house.

1123
01:20:02,882 --> 01:20:05,133
(LAUGHlNG)

1124
01:20:07,511 --> 01:20:09,971
They are not good boys anymore.

1125
01:20:10,389 --> 01:20:12,223
They're killers now.

1126
01:20:12,349 --> 01:20:13,850
Cold as stone.

1127
01:20:15,227 --> 01:20:16,478
l know.

1128
01:20:16,770 --> 01:20:19,981
l know what they were and what they are,
and it's not about that.

1129
01:20:20,065 --> 01:20:23,776
lt's not worth it,
throwing away life just to get even.

1130
01:20:24,945 --> 01:20:27,280
You and the lawyer
have a chance to get out.

1131
01:20:27,364 --> 01:20:28,740
To get out the right way.

1132
01:20:28,824 --> 01:20:31,159
There's no choice. Not for us.

1133
01:20:35,539 --> 01:20:37,707
SHAKES: On occasion,
I'd have dinner with Carol.

1134
01:20:37,791 --> 01:20:41,753
She still lived in the neighborhood,
and was a social worker in the South Bronx.

1135
01:20:41,837 --> 01:20:45,215
Her concern for us
was undiminished by the passing years.

1136
01:20:45,299 --> 01:20:48,843
Whenever we went out as a group,
she'd walk between Michael and John,

1137
01:20:48,928 --> 01:20:50,845
grasping their arms,

1138
01:20:51,305 --> 01:20:53,473
in step between the lawyer and the killer.

1139
01:20:53,557 --> 01:20:57,477
Mug me or marry me, Shakes.
l'm too tired for anything else.

1140
01:20:58,270 --> 01:21:01,064
Won't you settle for a couple of beers?

1141
01:21:02,399 --> 01:21:04,526
lf that's your best offer.

1142
01:21:05,611 --> 01:21:07,987
l'll throw in a hug and a kiss.

1143
01:21:08,280 --> 01:21:09,489
Deal.

1144
01:21:13,077 --> 01:21:14,744
(UPBEAT MUSlC PLAYlNG)

1145
01:21:15,120 --> 01:21:17,330
-You look tired.
-Thank you.

1146
01:21:18,582 --> 01:21:22,418
They don't give you time to sleep
in this new job of yours?

1147
01:21:25,548 --> 01:21:27,674
So, how much do you know?

1148
01:21:28,008 --> 01:21:30,385
Just what the neighborhood says.

1149
01:21:30,469 --> 01:21:33,179
And what l read in papers like yours.

1150
01:21:33,347 --> 01:21:34,847
What does the neighborhood say?

1151
01:21:34,932 --> 01:21:37,100
That they're gonna put
Johnny and Tommy away.

1152
01:21:37,184 --> 01:21:39,561
That their best friend's gonna be
the one to do it.

1153
01:21:39,645 --> 01:21:42,355
-You believe that?
-lt's hard not to.

1154
01:21:42,439 --> 01:21:46,276
Unless we all have it wrong.
He did take the fucking case.

1155
01:21:47,027 --> 01:21:50,697
-He did take the case.
-Then what else is there to say?

1156
01:21:52,116 --> 01:21:55,785
You know Michael very well,
maybe even better than l do.

1157
01:21:56,370 --> 01:21:59,122
Yeah, l thought l did. Now, l don't know.

1158
01:21:59,331 --> 01:22:01,499
-You do know.
-l don't know!

1159
01:22:01,584 --> 01:22:03,585
He went in there and he asked for the case!

1160
01:22:03,669 --> 01:22:06,296
Now, you tell me,
what the hell kind of friend is that?

1161
01:22:06,380 --> 01:22:08,006
The best kind.

1162
01:22:08,591 --> 01:22:12,385
The kind who'll throw away everything
to help his friends.

1163
01:22:15,139 --> 01:22:17,265
What are you telling me?

1164
01:22:18,017 --> 01:22:22,228
You know this neighborhood, Carol.
Everything's a shakedown or a scam.

1165
01:22:22,313 --> 01:22:24,856
Why should this be any different?

1166
01:22:30,029 --> 01:22:31,487
l'm hungry.

1167
01:22:32,531 --> 01:22:34,949
l'm gonna get something to eat.

1168
01:22:35,534 --> 01:22:39,203
There's this point in Michael
that you can't go beyond.

1169
01:22:39,788 --> 01:22:42,040
l mean, you can try. l tried.

1170
01:22:43,167 --> 01:22:45,835
And he just shut down.

1171
01:22:46,462 --> 01:22:49,839
Couldn't touch him,
couldn't even breathe on him.

1172
01:22:53,093 --> 01:22:55,011
l thought it was me.

1173
01:22:56,263 --> 01:22:59,599
After a while, it just gets easier to let it go.

1174
01:22:59,683 --> 01:23:02,894
-Do you still love him?
-l don't think about it.

1175
01:23:04,146 --> 01:23:06,189
lf l did, l'd say yes.

1176
