Overruled.

1412
01:39:36,346 --> 01:39:37,346
(SNYDER CLEARlNG THROAT)

1413
01:39:37,430 --> 01:39:40,724
Mrs. Salinas, what time did you have lunch?

1414
01:39:41,351 --> 01:39:44,436
-About 1:30.
-And what did you have for lunch?

1415
01:39:44,520 --> 01:39:47,356
MRS. SALlNAS: lt was a while ago.
Probably a salad.

1416
01:39:47,440 --> 01:39:49,650
l like to eat a little light in the day.

1417
01:39:49,734 --> 01:39:52,944
A martini, two glasses of wine,
and a salad. ls that correct?

1418
01:39:53,029 --> 01:39:54,780
Yes, that's right.

1419
01:39:54,864 --> 01:39:59,618
And then you had wine at dinner,
about six hours later. ls that right?

1420
01:39:59,702 --> 01:40:01,036
MRS. SALlNAS: Yes, that's right.

1421
01:40:01,120 --> 01:40:02,871
How much wine did you have to drink

1422
01:40:02,955 --> 01:40:05,457
by the time my clients allegedly
walked into McHale's?

1423
01:40:05,541 --> 01:40:09,378
-Two glasses.
-Would you say that four glasses of wine

1424
01:40:10,004 --> 01:40:14,091
and a martini within a six-hour period
is a lot for you to drink?

1425
01:40:14,175 --> 01:40:15,676
Yes, it is.

1426
01:40:21,599 --> 01:40:25,852
Have you ever heard a gun fired,
prior to the night in question?

1427
01:40:26,396 --> 01:40:27,562
No.

1428
01:40:29,232 --> 01:40:33,568
-How would you describe the sound?
-lt was loud. Like fireworks loud.

1429
01:40:35,196 --> 01:40:39,157
-Did the sound frighten you?
-MRS. SALlNAS: Very much.

1430
01:40:39,951 --> 01:40:42,035
Did you close your eyes?

1431
01:40:43,621 --> 01:40:46,707
At first, until the shooting stopped.
Then l opened them.

1432
01:40:46,791 --> 01:40:51,336
Did you think the men who did the shooting
were going to kill everybody in McHale's?

1433
01:40:51,421 --> 01:40:55,549
l really didn't know what to think.
l just knew that the man had been shot.

1434
01:40:55,633 --> 01:41:00,137
Did you think you might be shot dead
by the two cold-blooded killers?

1435
01:41:01,013 --> 01:41:02,389
Yes, l did.

1436
01:41:02,473 --> 01:41:06,768
Yet despite that fear,
despite that risk to your life,

1437
01:41:06,894 --> 01:41:10,856
you looked at their faces as they left?

1438
01:41:12,066 --> 01:41:14,401
-Yes, l did.
-ls that correct?

1439
01:41:15,445 --> 01:41:16,862
Yes, l did.

1440
01:41:17,071 --> 01:41:19,948
Did you look at their faces? Did you

1441
01:41:20,032 --> 01:41:23,160
really look, Mrs. Salinas?

1442
01:41:24,454 --> 01:41:27,414
l glanced at them when they walked by,
but l did see them.

1443
01:41:27,498 --> 01:41:29,624
You glanced?

1444
01:41:30,084 --> 01:41:31,835
You didn't look?

1445
01:41:32,295 --> 01:41:34,004
l saw them.

1446
01:41:34,756 --> 01:41:37,257
You glanced at them, Mrs. Salinas.

1447
01:41:37,341 --> 01:41:41,303
You glanced at them through the eyes
of a very frightened woman

1448
01:41:41,387 --> 01:41:44,181
who maybe had too much to drink.

1449
01:41:44,891 --> 01:41:47,601
-Objection, Your Honor.
-SNYDER: There is no need, Your Honor.

1450
01:41:47,685 --> 01:41:49,269
l have no further questions.

1451
01:41:49,353 --> 01:41:52,314
WElSMAN: Thank you, Mrs. Salinas.
You may step down.

1452
01:41:55,693 --> 01:41:57,778
SHAKES: It was 6:15 on Sunday morning.

1453
01:41:57,862 --> 01:42:01,031
Frank Magcicco worked
out of a homicide unit in Brooklyn.

1454
01:42:01,115 --> 01:42:05,118
He was a first-grade detective
with an honest name and a solid reputation.

1455
01:42:05,203 --> 01:42:07,496
He was also King Benny's nephew.

1456
01:42:07,580 --> 01:42:10,499
Nick Davenport was with Internal Affairs.

1457
01:42:10,583 --> 01:42:13,502
He was ambitious and wanted
to make captain before he hit 40.

1458
01:42:13,586 --> 01:42:15,462
He knew the fastest way up the track

1459
01:42:15,546 --> 01:42:19,549
was to reel in a maximum amount
of dirty cops in a minimum amount of time.

1460
01:42:19,634 --> 01:42:21,343
Frank, what is this shit?

1461
01:42:21,427 --> 01:42:23,345
lf l were you, l'd do what the kid says.

1462
01:42:23,429 --> 01:42:27,265
You make this, you'll be having breakfast
once a month with the Commissioner.

1463
01:42:27,391 --> 01:42:30,894
You got a real hard-on for this Styler guy.
What's your beef with him?

1464
01:42:30,978 --> 01:42:32,771
-One more thing.
-l can't wait.

1465
01:42:32,897 --> 01:42:37,651
lt's simple. No one knows who fed you
this information. And l mean nobody.

1466
01:42:38,069 --> 01:42:39,277
How did you get it?

1467
01:42:39,403 --> 01:42:42,906
lt fell into my lap.
Just like it's gonna fall into yours.

1468
01:42:49,163 --> 01:42:50,914
NlCK: Christ Almighty.

1469
01:42:58,089 --> 01:43:02,092
-You got everything here but a confession.
-SHAKES: l thought l'd leave that up to you.

1470
01:43:02,176 --> 01:43:04,302
My preference is that you beat it out of him.

1471
01:43:04,428 --> 01:43:05,929
There's even surveillance photos.

1472
01:43:06,013 --> 01:43:09,766
This piece of shit's pulling in about
$5,000 a month, ripping off pushers.

1473
01:43:09,851 --> 01:43:12,102
-Has been for about three years.
-More like four.

1474
01:43:12,186 --> 01:43:14,813
-He ain't gonna see five.
-Got enough for a conviction?

1475
01:43:14,939 --> 01:43:17,816
That ain't up to me. That's up to a jury.

1476
01:43:20,611 --> 01:43:22,445
SHAKES: Show the jury this.

1477
01:43:24,699 --> 01:43:26,408
What do you got there, Ness?

1478
01:43:26,492 --> 01:43:28,910
About three weeks ago,
the body of a drug dealer

1479
01:43:28,995 --> 01:43:32,372
named lndian Red Lopez was found
in an alley in Jackson Heights.

1480
01:43:32,456 --> 01:43:34,833
Three bullets in his head,
nothing in his pockets.

1481
01:43:34,959 --> 01:43:36,126
l'm with you so far.

1482
01:43:36,210 --> 01:43:39,129
This is the gun that killed him,
and these are the shells.

1483
01:43:40,631 --> 01:43:42,674
What's behind door number three?

1484
01:43:42,800 --> 01:43:45,719
The prints on the gun
belong to Adam Styler.

1485
01:43:49,140 --> 01:43:51,391
-(LAUGHS) Do me a favor, will you?
-What's that?

1486
01:43:51,475 --> 01:43:54,436
lf l ever make it onto your shit list,
give me a call.

1487
01:43:54,520 --> 01:43:56,855
Give me a chance to apologize.

1488
01:43:57,064 --> 01:43:59,482
SHAKES: So you need anything else,
you talk to Frank.

1489
01:43:59,567 --> 01:44:02,944
-He knows how to get a hold of me.
-Take care of yourself, kid.

1490
01:44:03,029 --> 01:44:06,656
-Water gets choppy out your way.
-l'll do what l can.

1491
01:44:09,535 --> 01:44:13,663
-Did you ever think of becoming a cop?
-And leave the good guys?

1492
01:44:31,098 --> 01:44:33,266
-The body of Christ.
-Amen.

1493
01:44:42,360 --> 01:44:44,361
The body of Christ.

1494
01:44:52,578 --> 01:44:53,954
Amen.

1495
01:44:56,916 --> 01:44:58,416
The body of Christ.

1496
01:45:01,921 --> 01:45:04,130
SHAKES: Michael had done
all that could be expected

1497
01:45:04,215 --> 01:45:07,634
of an Assistant District Attorney
seeking a conviction.

1498
01:45:07,718 --> 01:45:12,263
He had a forensic expert detail the make
and caliber of the gun that killed Nokes.

1499
01:45:12,390 --> 01:45:15,225
He just never had the murder weapon
to present as evidence.

1500
01:45:15,309 --> 01:45:18,728
And he never gave the jury
a motive for the murder.

1501
01:45:19,146 --> 01:45:21,773
The tension of his task,
the hours he was working,

1502
01:45:21,899 --> 01:45:24,901
and the uncertainty about the outcome
weighed heavily on him.

1503
01:45:24,986 --> 01:45:26,319
Did you see their faces?

1504
01:45:26,404 --> 01:45:29,155
Yes, l looked at them,
and they looked at me.

1505
01:45:29,240 --> 01:45:30,615
Did they say anything to you?

1506
01:45:30,741 --> 01:45:33,326
No, they just looked at me
and walked out of McHale's.

1507
01:45:33,411 --> 01:45:35,829
Are you sure the two defendants
killed Sean Nokes?

1508
01:45:35,913 --> 01:45:37,330
l know they killed him.

1509
01:45:37,415 --> 01:45:40,333
SHAKES: If the plan worked,
it would be everyone's success.

1510
01:45:40,418 --> 01:45:42,627
If it failed, the fault would fall to Michael.

1511
01:45:46,132 --> 01:45:50,051
Father Bobby Carillo, the priest with
the best hook shot on the West Side,

1512
01:45:50,136 --> 01:45:54,097
remained the key to a plan that called
for all involved to get away with murder.

1513
01:45:54,223 --> 01:45:58,018
Did you turn around, look behind you,
when you heard the shooting, Mr. Carson?

1514
01:45:58,102 --> 01:46:00,145
Why didn't you turn around, Mr. Carson?

1515
01:46:00,271 --> 01:46:02,814
l was concerned for my companion's safety.

1516
01:46:02,940 --> 01:46:05,108
Did the two individuals
threaten you in any way?

1517
01:46:05,234 --> 01:46:06,276
No.

1518
01:46:06,402 --> 01:46:10,572
Did they threaten anyone
in McHale's Restaurant, as far as you know?

1519
01:46:10,656 --> 01:46:12,323
MR. CARSON: l didn't see it, but l know it.

1520
01:46:12,450 --> 01:46:15,285
SNYDER: If you didn't see the defendants
shoot the guy,

1521
01:46:15,411 --> 01:46:18,621
then how do you know
it was the defendants that shot him?

1522
01:46:41,353 --> 01:46:43,313
What's the emergency?

1523
01:46:46,817 --> 01:46:49,402
Shakes shouldn't have sent you.
lt's too risky.

1524
01:46:49,487 --> 01:46:52,489
Nobody sent me. l wanted to see you.

1525
01:46:54,658 --> 01:46:55,825
Why?

1526
01:46:57,036 --> 01:47:00,080
Shakes met with Father Bobby
two weeks ago.

1527
01:47:00,164 --> 01:47:04,834
-He hasn't heard from him since.
-lt's not an overnight decision for him.

1528
01:47:07,213 --> 01:47:11,382
-What if he doesn't testify?
-Then we got a very serious problem.

1529
01:47:26,023 --> 01:47:28,858
Have Shakes talk to Father Bobby again.

1530
01:47:30,194 --> 01:47:34,114
Have him tell him the whole story.
He'll know what that means.

1531
01:47:34,198 --> 01:47:35,865
He already has.

1532
01:47:36,867 --> 01:47:38,076
What?

1533
01:47:40,579 --> 01:47:43,748
l was with him
when he talked to Father Bobby.

1534
01:47:45,918 --> 01:47:48,211
l heard everything, Michael.

1535
01:47:57,930 --> 01:47:59,556
So you know.

1536
01:48:01,892 --> 01:48:03,226
Yeah.

1537
01:48:07,189 --> 01:48:09,107
lf only you'd told me...

1538
01:48:13,737 --> 01:48:16,573
l think things could've been different.

1539
01:48:18,075 --> 01:48:20,076
lf you could've talked.

1540
01:48:24,582 --> 01:48:26,624
(CRYlNG) Maybe...

1541
01:48:53,777 --> 01:48:55,278
(JAZZ MUSlC PLAYlNG)

1542
01:48:55,362 --> 01:48:56,863
Hey, how you doing?

1543
01:48:56,947 --> 01:49:00,950
Carmine, that diet is working.
l don't care what anybody says.

1544
01:49:02,411 --> 01:49:06,372
-You still have a thing for Doris Day.
-She was a good woman.

1545
01:49:07,708 --> 01:49:09,626
You know the strega?

1546
01:49:10,085 --> 01:49:13,379
lt's hard to miss a lady
with four warts and only one eye.

1547
01:49:13,464 --> 01:49:15,798
She needs the heads.

1548
01:49:21,305 --> 01:49:23,431
Take this to the witch.

1549
01:49:24,308 --> 01:49:26,226
Now, why does she need the heads?

1550
01:49:26,310 --> 01:49:29,145
-She takes the eyes.
-Wonderful.

1551
01:49:29,230 --> 01:49:32,982
Puts them in a bowl and mixes them
with water and oil.

1552
01:49:33,317 --> 01:49:34,817
And then?

1553
01:49:36,153 --> 01:49:38,947
People get headaches, they go to her.

1554
01:49:39,114 --> 01:49:42,075
She looks into their eyes and tells them

1555
01:49:42,159 --> 01:49:44,244
who is wishing the headaches.

1556
01:49:44,328 --> 01:49:48,164
She says a few words
and the headaches go away.

1557
01:49:48,624 --> 01:49:52,961
Once in a while the person who wishes
the headaches goes away, too.

1558
01:49:53,963 --> 01:49:57,507
This guy, Addison,
the one who works for the Mayor,

1559
01:49:57,800 --> 01:50:00,176
he quits his job in two weeks.

1560
01:50:00,761 --> 01:50:04,347
He don't want nobody to know
what kind of a guy he is.

1561
01:50:04,431 --> 01:50:08,518
He don't want nobody to see
pictures of him they shouldn't see.

1562
01:50:09,019 --> 01:50:11,145
-He knows this?
-He will.

1563
01:50:12,439 --> 01:50:14,774
The boys he buys for parties are expensive.

1564
01:50:14,858 --> 01:50:18,820
Now, Addison makes good money,
but he don't make real money.

1565
01:50:19,780 --> 01:50:21,197
How much does he owe?

1566
01:50:21,282 --> 01:50:24,784
$8,000 with a heavy vig. l paid that off.

1567
01:50:25,494 --> 01:50:26,869
You paid?

1568
01:50:27,496 --> 01:50:30,039
Addison's debts belong to me now.

1569
01:50:31,125 --> 01:50:33,793
-You hate debts.
-l hate Addison.

1570
01:50:36,380 --> 01:50:40,133
We're in the dirty end of the field now.
That's where l play.

1571
01:50:40,217 --> 01:50:42,302
And l like to play alone.

1572
01:50:42,386 --> 01:50:46,681
You're a nice kid. You always were.
Don't let this change it.

1573
01:51:00,362 --> 01:51:03,156
SHAKES: His mother named him
Edward Goldenberg Robinson

1574
01:51:03,240 --> 01:51:05,408
after her favorite actor.

1575
01:51:05,534 --> 01:51:07,327
To continue the Hollywood connection

1576
01:51:07,411 --> 01:51:10,163
Eddie Robinson took the street name
Little Caesar

1577
01:51:10,247 --> 01:51:13,750
as he made his way up the ranks
of the lucrative drug trade.

1578
01:51:13,834 --> 01:51:17,503
He had a 12-year-old son
in a private school in upstate New York.

1579
01:51:17,588 --> 01:51:20,173
He named him Rizzo,
after his youngest brother,

1580
01:51:20,257 --> 01:51:24,010
who died while in the custody
of the Wilkinson Home for Boys.

1581
01:51:24,094 --> 01:51:27,263
-l want you to give me some money.
-All right.

1582
01:51:27,806 --> 01:51:29,515
l'll play along.

1583
01:51:29,808 --> 01:51:33,644
-How long before you pay it back?
-l ain't paying it back.

1584
01:51:33,729 --> 01:51:35,521
Somebody else is.

1585
01:51:37,608 --> 01:51:39,192
This somebody l know?

1586
01:51:39,276 --> 01:51:42,612
-Your little brother knew him.
-Rizzo?

1587
01:51:45,366 --> 01:51:47,033
How did he know Rizzo?

1588
01:51:47,117 --> 01:51:51,412
Henry Addison was a guard
in an upstate reform school.

1589
01:51:52,081 --> 01:51:56,125
He was there the same time as Rizzo,
before and after he died.

1590
01:52:02,007 --> 01:52:04,926
Count out $8,000, put it in an envelope.

1591
01:52:10,724 --> 01:52:13,101
You go back a long time, old man.

1592
01:52:14,144 --> 01:52:15,978
Old men always do.

1593
01:52:16,105 --> 01:52:19,023
Ran with the guineas
back when the guineas were tough.

1594
01:52:19,108 --> 01:52:20,942
l ran when l could.

1595
01:52:21,610 --> 01:52:23,778
Looked good doing it, too.

1596
01:52:23,862 --> 01:52:25,988
(CHUCKLlNG)

1597
01:52:26,073 --> 01:52:29,867
Gave the business some style, some class.

1598
01:52:31,078 --> 01:52:35,540
Made it a call for respect
the way you wore it, the way you talked it.

1599
01:52:36,291 --> 01:52:38,709
l always liked that about you.

1600
01:52:38,794 --> 01:52:42,046
l'm no help to you. My tailor is dead.

1601
01:52:49,221 --> 01:52:53,307
l'll look up our friend
and collect the money he owes me.

1602
01:52:53,725 --> 01:52:58,604
-He owes you something more than money.
-Ain't nothing worth more than the green.

1603
01:52:58,939 --> 01:53:01,482
-This is.
-What, old man?

1604
01:53:02,359 --> 01:53:05,278
What's this guy owe
that means more than dollars?

1605
01:53:05,362 --> 01:53:09,323
He owes you Rizzo.
He's the man that killed your brother.

1606
01:53:18,750 --> 01:53:21,961
-They said he died of pneumonia.
-They said.

1607
01:53:29,553 --> 01:53:31,554
WElSMAN: What is the relevance of this?

1608
01:53:31,638 --> 01:53:34,432
So Ralph Ferguson
is a Sunday school teacher.

1609
01:53:34,516 --> 01:53:38,102
l don't know, Counsel.
What you're asking is highly unusual.

1610
01:53:38,187 --> 01:53:42,940
l understand that, Your Honor.
Again, l need to put a face to the victim.

1611
01:53:43,609 --> 01:53:47,153
Otherwise, it's just another name
in the obituaries.

1612
01:53:47,613 --> 01:53:49,822
Mr. Snyder, any objections?

1613
01:53:51,241 --> 01:53:53,034
l don't have a problem with it.

1614
01:53:53,744 --> 01:53:58,539
Your Honor, the prosecution would like
to call Ralph Ferguson to the stand.

1615
01:54:23,941 --> 01:54:26,400
-Good morning, Mr. Ferguson.
-Good morning.

1616
01:54:26,485 --> 01:54:30,279
l thank you for coming.
l realize, for you, this has been a long trip.

1617
01:54:30,364 --> 01:54:33,616
l'm just sorry it had to be
for something like this.

1618
01:54:33,700 --> 01:54:36,202
You and the victim, Sean Nokes,
were good friends.

1619
01:54:36,286 --> 01:54:39,330
Your testimony as a character witness
will be very valuable.

1620
01:54:39,414 --> 01:54:42,833
We were great friends.
lt would be hard to find a better friend.

1621
01:54:42,918 --> 01:54:47,463
-Would you say you were his best friend?
-l was his closest, that's for sure.

1622
01:54:47,548 --> 01:54:51,592
-How long did you know each other?
-About 17, 18 years.

1623
01:54:52,135 --> 01:54:55,513
-Did you see each other often?
-As often as we could.

1624
01:54:55,597 --> 01:54:59,392
Weekends, holidays, vacations,
things like that.

1625
01:55:00,519 --> 01:55:04,105
-What kind of man was Sean Nokes?
-He was a good man.

1626
01:55:04,189 --> 01:55:07,233
He was too good to be shot dead
by a couple of street punks.

1627
01:55:07,317 --> 01:55:09,694
Objection.
Statement is one of opinion, not fact.

1628
01:55:09,778 --> 01:55:13,406
-He was asked his opinion.
-Overruled. Please proceed.

1629
01:55:15,284 --> 01:55:19,453
Mr. Ferguson, were you aware
of any enemies he might have had?

1630
01:55:19,913 --> 01:55:22,081
Sean Nokes had no enemies.

1631
01:55:22,332 --> 01:55:25,876
Thank you, Mr. Ferguson.
l have no further questions.

1632
01:55:30,132 --> 01:55:31,924
SNYDER: What is that, a prison?

1633
01:55:32,009 --> 01:55:34,427
FERGUSON: No,
it's a juvenile facility for young boys.

1634
01:55:34,511 --> 01:55:37,638
Your function was what
at this juvenile facility?

1635
01:55:37,723 --> 01:55:39,307
Standard stuff.

1636
01:55:39,600 --> 01:55:43,644
Keep the boys in line,
make sure they got to class on time,

1637
01:55:44,104 --> 01:55:47,857
keep an eye out for trouble, put them down
for the night. Nothing exciting.

1638
01:55:47,941 --> 01:55:50,735
As guards, were you and Mr. Nokes allowed

1639
